{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1976, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer array groups, where groups[i] represents the size of the i^th group. You are also given an integer array elements.\nYour task is to assign one element to each group based on the following rules:\n\nAn element at index j can be assigned to a group i if groups[i] is divisible by elements[j].\nIf there are multiple elements that can be assigned, assign the element with the smallest index j.\nIf no element satisfies the condition for a group, assign -1 to that group.\n\nReturn an integer array assigned, where assigned[i] is the index of the element chosen for group i, or -1 if no suitable element exists.\nNote: An element may be assigned to more than one group.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: groups = [8,4,3,2,4], elements = [4,2]\nOutput: [0,0,-1,1,0]\nExplanation:\n\nelements[0] = 4 is assigned to groups 0, 1, and 4.\nelements[1] = 2 is assigned to group 3.\nGroup 2 cannot be assigned any element.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: groups = [2,3,5,7], elements = [5,3,3]\nOutput: [-1,1,0,-1]\nExplanation:\n\nelements[1] = 3 is assigned to group 1.\nelements[0] = 5 is assigned to group 2.\nGroups 0 and 3 cannot be assigned any element.\n\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: groups = [10,21,30,41], elements = [2,1]\nOutput: [0,1,0,1]\nExplanation:\nelements[0] = 2 is assigned to the groups with even values, and elements[1] = 1 is assigned to the groups with odd values.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= groups.length <= 10^5\n1 <= elements.length <= 10^5\n1 <= groups[i] <= 10^5\n1 <= elements[i] <= 10^5\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def assignElements(self, groups: List[int], elements: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 2042, "char_start": 1988, "quote": "Input:\n[8, 4, 3, 2, 4]\n[4, 2]\nOutput:\n[0, 0, -1, 1, 0]", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 2106, "char_start": 2054, "quote": "Input:\n[2, 3, 5, 7]\n[5, 3, 3]\nOutput:\n[-1, 1, 0, -1]", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 2169, "char_start": 2118, "quote": "Input:\n[10, 21, 30, 41]\n[2, 1]\nOutput:\n[0, 1, 0, 1]", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "c310aecc3c343d26db53bc34a7f80464e9f86d3416f0765712d0a1743bb38432", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "7d746c830e8c8b9dcf8f3dcfe925323c8ad9b975567b6ccd780e7fb3674a5575", "seq": 2}
